# Companion to bind-mount-auto.conf.example - exercises the *explicit*
# WORKSPACE_USER path instead of the auto-default one: proves a value
# already set in the profile is honored as-is and not overwritten by
# `nix run .#up`'s "fill it in if empty" logic (see the WORKSPACE_USER
# comment in flake.nix's `up`/`reset-workspace` apps).
#
# SECURITY WARNING - read .env.example's own WORKSPACE_HOST_PATH comment
# before pointing this at anything but a disposable scratch directory:
# it's a bind mount into the one container that runs agent-issued shell
# commands unreviewed, so the agent gets real read/write access to
# whatever host path you set here. This profile defaults to
# .bind-mount-scratch/explicit-user specifically because that's
# throwaway - if you copy this as a starting point for a real profile,
# don't reuse a directory you care about.
#
# Usage (from the repo root):
#
#   cp scripts/test-profiles/bind-mount-explicit-user.conf.example ./bind-mount-explicit-user.conf
#   mkdir -p .bind-mount-scratch/explicit-user
#   id -u; id -g   # note these, or run: printf '%s:%s\n' "$(id -u)" "$(id -g)"
#   # paste that as WORKSPACE_USER below - it has to be your own uid:gid
#   # (or whoever's going to own .bind-mount-scratch/explicit-user), or the
#   # write check in validate-workspace-bind-mount.sh will correctly fail
#   # with a permission error, same as any other uid/host-directory mismatch
#   # would.
#   # fill in ANTHROPIC_API_KEY below too (blank is fine if you're only
#   # running validate-workspace-bind-mount.sh)
#   nix run .#up -- ./bind-mount-explicit-user.conf
#   sh scripts/validate-workspace-bind-mount.sh ./bind-mount-explicit-user.conf
#   nix run .#down -- ./bind-mount-explicit-user.conf
#
# ./bind-mount-explicit-user.conf (once copied) is gitignored, same as
# .env - this .example template is the only copy meant to be committed.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

WORKSPACE_HOST_PATH=./.bind-mount-scratch/explicit-user
WORKSPACE_REPO_PATH=/repo
# Fill in with your own `id -u`:`id -g` (see above) - deliberately set
# explicitly rather than left for auto-detect.
WORKSPACE_USER=
